CHAPTER I GENERAL PROVISIONS

Article 1 (Purpose) The purpose of this Act is to efficiently promote the construction of Daegu-Gyeongbuk Integrated New Airport and the development of the previous site by prescribing matters necessary for the construction of the Daegu-Gyeongbuk Integrated New Airport and the development of the previous site by, thereby contributing to the balanced development of national land and the strengthening of national competitiveness.

Article 2 (Definitions) The terms used in this Act are defined as follows: <Amended on Jan. 31, 2025>
  1. The term "Daegu-Gyeongbuk Integrated New Airport" (hereinafter referred to as "integrated new airport") means an airport constructed by relocating Daegu military air base defined in subparagraph 1 of Article 2 of the Special Act on the Relocation of Military Air Bases and Support Therefor (hereinafter referred to as a "military air base") and Daegu International Airport designated and publicly notified pursuant to subparagraph 3 of Article 2 of the Airport Facilities Act;
  2. The term "integrated new airport construction project" means the following projects for the construction of the integrated new airport:
  a. A military air base relocation project under the Special Act on the Relocation of Military Air Bases and Support Therefor (hereinafter referred to as a "military air base relocation project") and a construction project of airport facilities under subparagraph 7 of Article 2 of the Airport Facilities Act;
  b. Construction of infrastructure such as means of access and transportation necessary for airport development, and creation of facilities related to airport services, such as convenience facilities, air cargo distribution facilities, information and communications facilities, etc. for airport users, persons engaged in aviation-related affairs, etc.;
  c. Creation of residential facilities for persons engaged in aviation-related affairs and persons, etc. who lose their residence due to the construction of the integrated new airport and of facilities for conveniences, etc. incidental thereto;
  3. The term "previous site" means an existing site where a military airbase and Daegu International Airport have been established;
  4. The term "area adjacent to the previous site" means an area adjacent to the previous site, which is designated and publicly notified pursuant to Presidential Decree because it is deemed necessary to require planned management, from among the areas adjacent to the previous site, which may be affected by the development of the previous site;
  5. The term "previous site development project" means a project to develop a city in which tourist facilities, commercial facilities, high-tech industrial facilities, residential facilities, etc. are combined by using the previous site;
  6. The term "local government of the previous site" means Daegu Metropolitan City in which a military air base and Daegu International Airport are located;
  7. The term "area adjacent to the relocation site of the integrated new airport" (hereinafter referred to as "area adjacent to the relocation site") means the area of Gunwoung-gun, Daegu Metropolitan City and Euseong-gun, Gyeongsangbuk-do, where the integrated new airport is to be built;
  8. The term "project for supporting the environs of the relocation site" means a project implemented by the Minister of National Defense and the head of the local government of the previous site after formulating a support plan pursuant to Article 11 of the Special Act on the Relocation of Military Air Bases and Support Therefor.

Article 3 (Basic direction) The State and a metropolitan local government shall construct an integrated new airport in a direction where the following characteristics can be realized and develop the previous site:
  1. An airport with combined functions centered on passengers and logistics, including the relocation of a military air base and private airports;
  2. Prompt construction of an airport which ensures the safety of runway management and aircraft operation;
  3. Balanced development of national land, which alleviates the concentration of the Seoul Metropolitan Area and revitalizes provinces;
  4. Creation of a city in which functions of tourism, commerce, industry, etc. are revitalized through the development of the previous site.

Article 4 (Responsibilities of the State and local governments) (1) The State and metropolitan local governments shall mutually cooperate in order to efficiently promote a project for constructing an integrated new airport and a project for developing the previous site, and shall endeavor to promote the project in a successful manner.
  (2) The State and metropolitan governments shall endeavor to formulate a financing plan, etc. and to reflect necessary financial resources so that the integrated new airport construction project and the previous site development project can be implemented in a stable manner.

Article 5 (Relationship with other statutes) (1) This Act shall take precedence over other statutes regarding the integrated new airport construction project and the previous site development project; provided, if any other statute has provisions more lenient than the special cases concerning the regulation under this Act, the provisions of those statutes shall apply.
  (2) Except as provided in this Act, the Special Act on the Relocation of Military Air Base Relocation and Support and the Act on National Defense and Military Installations Projects shall apply to military air base relocation projects.
  (3) Except as provided for in this Act, the Airport Facilities Act shall apply to airport development projects under the Airport Facilities Act.
  (4) Except as provided for in this Act, relevant statutes such as the National Land Planning and Utilization Act, the Urban Development Act, the Industrial Sites and Development Act, the Regional Development Assistance Act, and the Housing Site Development Promotion Act, shall apply to the previous site development project.

Article 6 (Relationship to other plans) Plans and implementation plans for the integrated new airport construction project and the previous site development project under this Act shall take precedence over plans under other Acts; provided, this shall not apply to the following plans:
  1. A comprehensive national land plan under Article 6(2)1 of the Framework Act on the National Land;
  2. A plan for national core transport network under Article 4 of the National Transport System Efficiency Act;
  3. A master plan for aviation policy under Article 3 of the Aviation Business Act;
  4. A comprehensive plan for airport development provided for in Article 3 of the Airport Facilities Act;
  5. An urban or Gun master plan defined in subparagraph 3 of Article 2 of the National Land Planning and Utilization Act;
  6. A management plan for protection zones, etc. referred to in Article 16 of the Protection of Military Bases and Installations Act.

CHAPTER II CONSTRUCTION OF AND SUPPORT FOR INTEGRATED NEW AIRPORTS

Article 7 (Implementation of projects for supporting environs of military air base relocation site) (1) Notwithstanding the State Property Act, the implementer of a military air base relocation project under Article 8(1) shall implement a support project for the environs of the relocation site within the limit of the amount calculated by subtracting the value of the newly constructed military air base from the value of the disused property, notwithstanding the State Property Act. In such cases, facilities installed as a support project for the environs of the relocation site shall be deemed included in the substitute facilities under Article 9(1) of the Special Act on Relocation of and Support for Military Air Base.
  (2) Notwithstanding the differential subsidy rate under Article 10 of the Subsidy Management Act, the head of the relevant central administrative agency may increase the National Treasury subsidy according to the subsidy rate prescribed by Presidential Decree for the projects for the development of the environs of the relocation site, which are prescribed by Presidential Decree, to the heads of local governments.
  (3) The implementer of a military air base relocation project under Article 8(1) may provide support necessary for the livelihood support, settlement, or stabilization of livelihood of migrants for migrants who have lost their livelihood due to the implementation of the military air base relocation project, as prescribed by Presidential Decree. In such cases, the implementer of a military air base relocation project, who is a public housing project operator under Article 4 of the Special Act on Public Housing, may supply public rental housing units under Article 2 of the Special Act on Public Housing, as prescribed by Presidential Decree, for the smooth settlement, etc. of migrants. <Amended on Jan. 31, 2025>
  (4) The Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport may subsidize the Housing and Urban Fund established under the Housing and Urban Fund Act for projects for the supply of public rental housing units under paragraph (3). <Added on Jan. 31, 2025>

Article 8 (Implementers of integrated new airport construction project) (1) The military air base relocation project from among the integrated new airport construction projects shall be implemented by the head of the local government of the previous site, and the airport development project under the Airport Facilities Act shall be implemented by the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport. <Amended on Jan. 31, 2025>
  (2) Where a person other than the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport intends to implement an airport development project under paragraph (1), the person shall obtain permission from the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport, as prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport.
  (3) The Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport may, if necessary for the efficient execution of integrated new airport construction project, entrust part of the airport development project under paragraph (1) to the head of the local government of the previous site or jointly execute such project, as prescribed by Presidential Decree. <Added on Jan. 31, 2025>
  (4) The head of the local government of the previous site may designate a project agent to vicariously perform the whole or part of the military air base relocation project and the project entrusted pursuant to paragraph (3) from among persons falling under any of the subparagraphs of Article 14; provided, where the head intends to designate a project agent to vicariously perform the project entrusted pursuant to paragraph (3), he or she shall consult with the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport in advance. <Added on Jan. 31, 2025>

Article 9 (Formulation and approval of project plans and implementation plans) (1) The implementer of a military air base relocation project under Article 8(1) shall prepare a project plan and implementation plan for the military air base relocation project and obtain approval therefor from the Minister of National Defense, and Articles 4 and 6 of the Act on National Defense and Military Installations Projects shall apply to procedures for the formulation, approval, and public notice of the project plan and implementation plan.
  (2) The implementer of an airport development project under Article 8 shall formulate an implementation plan before commencing the airport development project, and Article 7 of the Airport Facilities Act shall apply to the procedures for formulating, approving, and publicly notifying the implementation plan.
  (3) With respect to environmental impact assessment under Article 22 of the Environmental Impact Assessment Act, an implementation plan under paragraph (1) or (2) shall be deemed an implementation plan under Article 6 of the National Defense and Military Installations Projects Act and Article 7 of the Airport Facilities Act, and the integrated new airport construction project shall be deemed a national defense and military installation project under subparagraph 2 of Article 2 of the Act on National Defense and Military Installations Projects and an airport development project under subparagraph 9 of Article 2 of the Airport Facilities Act.

Article 9-2 (Special cases concerning expropriation of land) (1) Where the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport formulates a master plan for airport development under Article 4 of the Airport Facilities Act, the Minister may include details of land, etc. (referring to land, goods, or rights under Article 12(1) of that Act; hereafter the same shall apply in this Article) to be included in the relevant project area.
  (2) Where the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport intends to include the details of land, etc. to be incorporated pursuant to paragraph (1) in the master plan for airport development, the Minister shall notify the owners and right holders of the relevant land, etc. of such fact.
  (3) Notwithstanding Article 12(2) of the Airport Facilities Act, project approval and public notice of project approval under Articles 20(1) and 22 of the Act on Acquisition of and Compensation for Land for Public Works Projects shall be deemed granted where a master plan for airport development is formulated and publicly notified, including the details of land, etc. to be incorporated pursuant to paragraph (1).
  (4) Where a public notice is given under paragraph (3), an application for adjudication on the expropriation or use of land, etc. may be filed within the project period specified in the master plan for airport development, notwithstanding Article 12(3) of the Airport Facilities Act.
  [Added on Jan. 31, 2025]

Article 10 (Legal fiction of authorization or permission) (1) Where the Minister of National Defense has granted approval of an implementation plan or approval of modification thereto under Article 9(1), the following permission, authorization, designation, approval, consultation, reporting, cancellation, decision, determination, consent, formulation, modification, etc. (hereinafter referred to as "authorization, permission, etc.") shall be deemed to have been granted, made, or obtained, and where approval of an implementation plan is publicly notified pursuant to that paragraph, authorization, permission, etc. under the following Acts shall be deemed publicly notified or announced; provided, subparagraph 16 shall be limited to national defense and military installations projects defined in subparagraph 1a through e of Article 2 of the Act on National Defense and Military Installations Projects:
  1. Permission to occupy or use public waters prescribed in Article 8 of the Public Waters Management and Reclamation Act, and approval for, or reporting on an implementation plan for occupation or use under Article 17 of that Act, or a license to reclaim public waters prescribed in Article 28 of that Act, and approval for a public water reclamation implementation plan prescribed in Article 38 of that Act;
  2. Permission for the implementation of development projects under Article 6(2) of the Airport Facilities Act and approval of the implementation plan under Article 7(3) of that Act;
  3. Permission for any development activity prescribed in Article 56 of the National Land Planning and Utilization Act;
  4. Permission for, consultation on diversion of farmland under Article 34 of the Farmland Act and permission for or temporarily using farmland for other purposes under Article 36 of that Act;
  5. Permission for, and reporting on, installation of emission facilities under Article 23 of the Clean Air Conservation Act;
  6. Permission to execute road works prescribed in Article 36 of the Road Act; or permission to occupy and use a road prescribed in Article 61 of that Act;
  7. Permission for, and reporting on, installation of discharging facilities under Article 33 of the Water Environment Conservation Act;
  8. Permission to build private roads under Article 4 of the Private Road Act;
  9. Permission to fell, etc. in lands for erosion control referred to in Article 14 of the Erosion Control Work Act and cancellation of designation of lands for erosion referred to in Article 20 of that Act;
  10. Permission for and reporting on activities within forest conservation zones under Article 9(2) of the Forest Protection Act and cancellation of designation of forest conservation zones under Article 11 of that Act;
  11. Permission for, or report on, felling, etc. of trees referred to in Article 36 of the Creation and Management of Forest Resources Act;
  12. Change and cancellation of preserved mountainous districts under Article 6 of the Mountainous Districts Management Act, permission for diversion of mountainous districts under Article 14 of that Act, and permission for or reporting on temporary use of mountainous districts under Article 15-2 of that Act;
  13. Permission for, and reporting on, installation of discharging facilities under Article 8 of the Noise and Vibration Control Act;
  14. Permission to occupy and use small rivers under Article 14 of the Small River Maintenance Act;
  15. Authorization to install private-use waterworks under Article 52 of the Water Supply and Waterworks Installation Act;
  16. Permission for acts in park areas under Article 23 of the Natural Parks Act;
  17. Permission for reburials of graves under Article 27 of the Act on Funeral Services;
  18. Approval or reporting of plans for works for establishing electric installations for private use under Article 8 of the Electrical Safety Management Act;
  19. Permission for diversion of grassland prescribed in Article 23 of the Grassland Act;
  20. Approval for or reporting on installation of a wastes disposal facility prescribed in Article 29 of the Wastes Control Act;
  21. Permission for works for public sewerage system under Article 16 of the Sewerage Act; permission for occupation of public sewerage systems under Article 24 of that Act; or report on installation of a private sewage treatment facility under Article 34(2) of that Act;
  22. Permission to occupy and use rivers under Article 33 of the River Act.
  (2) Where the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport formulates or approves the modification of the implementation plan pursuant to Article 9(2), it shall be deemed that the following approval, permission, authorization, determination, designation, license, consultation, agreement, deliberation or cancellation, etc. (hereinafter referred to as "authorization, permission, etc.") has been made; and where the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport publicly notifies the formulation or approval of the implementation plan pursuant to that Article, it shall be deemed that the public notification or public announcement of authorization, permission, etc., under the following statutes has been made:
  1. Deliberation by the Construction Technology Deliberative Committee under Article 5 of the Construction Technology Promotion Act;
  2. Deliberation by the Building Committee under Article 4 of the Building Act, building permits under Article 11 of that Act, building reports under Article 14 of that Act, permits and reports on change of use under Article 19 of that Act, permission to construct temporary structures under Article 20(1) of that Act, and reports under paragraph (3) of that Article, and consultation with the permitting authority under Article 29 of that Act;
  3. Approval of the implementation plan referred to in Article 9 of the Special Act on Designation and Management of Free Economic Zones;
  4. Permission to extract aggregate referred to in Article 22 of the Aggregate Extraction Act;
  5. Permission to occupy or use public waters and public notice of permission to occupy or use public waters referred to in Article 8 of the Public Waters Management and Reclamation Act, approval of or report on an implementation plan for occupancy or use of public waters referred to in Article 17 of that Act, reclamation license for public waters referred to in Article 28 of that Act, public notice of reclamation license referred to in Article 33 of that Act, consultation with the reclamation license agency or approval of such agency referred to in Article 35 of that Act, and approval of the implementation plan for reclamation of public waters referred to in 38 of that Act;
  6. Determination of urban or Gun management plans referred to in Article 30 of the National Land Planning and Utilization Act, permission to engage in development activities referred to in Article 56 of that Act, designation of implementers of urban or Gun planning facility projects referred to in Article 86 of that Act, authorization for implementation plans referred to in Article 88 of that Act, and public notice of an implementation plan referred to in Article 91 of that Act;
  7. Consultation on permission, etc. of an administrative agency referred to in Article 13 of the Protection of Military Bases and Installations Act;
  8. Permission for or consultation about conversion of farmland under Article 34 of the Farmland Act;
  9. Permission for, or report on, the establishment of emission facilities referred to in Article 23 of the Clean Air Conservation Act, Article 33 of the Water Environment Conservation Act, and Article 8 of the Noise and Vibration Control Act;
  10. Consultation with or approval of the road management agency referred to in Article 107 of the Road Act (only referring to those regarding the designation and public notice of road routes referred to in Article 19 of that Act, determination of road zones referred to in Article 25 of that Act, permission to implement road construction for persons other than the road management agency referred to in Article 36 of that Act, and permission to occupy roads referred to in Article 61(1) of that Act);
  11. Permission to occupy urban parks referred to in Article 24 of the Act on Urban Parks and Green Areas;
  12. Submission and review of statements of traffic impact assessment referred to in Article 16 of the Urban Traffic Improvement Promotion Act;
  13. Approval of urban railroads project plan referred to in Article 7 (1) of the Urban Railroad Act and license for urban railroads transport projects referred to in Article 26(1) of that Act;
  14. A permit to cut trees or perform other activities on land treated for erosion or collapse control under Article 14 of the Erosion Control Work Act, or cancellation of designation of land treated for erosion or collapse control under Article 20 of that Act;
  15. Cancellation of designation of forest conservation zones under Article 11 of the Forest Protection Act;
  16. Permission for, or report on, felling, etc. of trees referred to in Article 36(1) and (5) of the Creation and Management of Forest Resources Act;
  17. Designation of the implementer of industrial complex development projects referred to in Article 16 of the Industrial Sites and Development Act and approval for implementation plans for national industrial complex development referred to in Article 17 of that Act;
  18. Approval of, and report on, construction, etc. of a factory referred to in Article 13 of the Industrial Cluster Development and Factory Establishment Act;
  19. Change or cancellation of preserved mountainous districts under Article 6 of the Mountainous Districts Management Act, cancellation of designation of restricted areas for diversion or temporary use of mountainous districts under Article 11 of that Act, permission for diversion of mountainous districts under Article 14 of that Act, and reporting on diversion of mountainous districts under Article 15 of that Act;
  20. Report on firefighting installation referred to in Article 13(1) of the Firefighting System Installation Business Act;
  21. Consent to building permission, etc. under Article 6(1) of the Act on Installation and Maintenance of Firefighting Systems;
  22. Authorization for general waterworks business referred to in Article 17(1) of the Water Supply and Waterworks Installation Act and authorization for building private-use waterworks and private-use industrial waterworks referred to in Article 52 and 54 of that Act;
  23. Permission to build factory, etc. referred to in Article 6(1) of the Act on the Safety Control of Hazardous Substances;
  24. Consultation with a park management agency referred to in Article 71(1) of the Natural Parks Act (only referring to consultation on the permission for acts in park areas referred to in Article 23 of that Act);
  25. Permission for reburials of unclaimed graves under Article 27(1) of the Act on Funeral Services;
  26. Permission for, report of, or consultation on the diversion of grassland under Article 23 of the Grassland Act;
  27. Approval for, or report on, the installation of waste treatment facilities referred to in Article 29(2) of the Wastes Control Act;
  28. Permission to construct or maintain public sewerage referred to in Article 16 of the Sewerage Act, permission for occupation and use regarding the acts of occupation and use referred to in Article 24 of that Act, and report on establishment, etc. of private sewage treatment facilities referred to in Article 34(2) of that Act;
  29. Consultation with, or approval of, the river management agency referred to in Article 6 of the River Act (only referring to those regarding the permission to implement river works referred to in Article 30 of that Act, permission to occupy and use rivers and public notice of permission for occupation and use referred to in Article 33 of that Act, and permission to use permits for river water referred to in Article 50 of that Act).
  (3) Articles 24 through 26 of the Framework Act on Administration shall apply to the effects, procedures, etc. of authorization, permission, etc. and the legal fiction of authorization, permission, etc. under paragraphs (1) and (2).

Article 11 (Designation of prearranged areas for environs development) (1) Where necessary to efficiently promote the integrated new airport construction project, the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport may designate a specific area within 10 kilometers from the boundary of the following areas in connection with the integrated new airport construction project, as a prearranged area for environs development:
  1. A planned project area publicly notified pursuant to Article 4(4) of the Act on National Defense and Military Installations Projects, which shall apply mutatis mutandis pursuant to Article 5(2);
  2. An area prearranged for airport and aerodrome development publicly notified pursuant to Article 4(5) of the Airport Facilities Act, which shall apply mutatis mutandis pursuant to Article 5(3).
  (2) Matters necessary for the scope of prearranged areas for environs development under paragraph (1), procedures for designation, implementation of environs development projects, etc. shall be prescribed by Presidential Decree.

Article 12 (Task force for of integrated new airport construction) (1) An integrated new airport construction task force (hereinafter referred to as the "task force") shall be established under the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport for the smooth promotion and efficient management of the integrated new airport construction project.
  (2) The Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport may request the heads of relevant central administrative agencies, the heads of metropolitan local governments, relevant institutions, corporations, organizations, and project implementers to dispatch public officials or executive officers and employees under their control, if necessary for the smooth performance of the affairs of the task force.
  (3) Except as provided in paragraphs (1) and (2), matters necessary for the composition and operation of the task force shall be prescribed by Presidential Decree.

Article 13 (Consultative body for integrated new airport construction) (1) The Minister of National Defense and the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport shall fully cooperate for the efficient promotion of a new airport construction project.
  (2) The Ministry of National Defense and the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport may establish and operate a consultative body for the smooth promotion of a new airport construction project.
  (3) Matters necessary for the composition, operation, etc. of the consultative body under paragraph (2) shall be prescribed by Presidential Decree.

CHAPTER III IMPLEMENTATION OF PREVIOUS SITE DEVELOPMENT PROJECTS

Article 14 (Implementers of previous site development projects) The implementer of a previous site development project (hereinafter referred to as "development project implementer") shall be any of the following persons:
  1. The State or a local government; provided, the State shall be limited to cases where the State implements a project pursuant to the relevant statutes referred to in Article 5(4);
  2. A public institution under the Act on the Management of Public Institutions;
  3. A local government-invested public corporation prescribed in the Local Public Enterprises Act;
  4. A corporation established for the purpose of implementing the previous site development project, the total investment ratio of which by a person falling under any of subparagraphs 1 through 3 exceeds 50/100.

Article 15 (Formulation of previous site development plan) (1) The development project implementer shall formulate a development plan for the previous site development project (hereinafter referred to as "development plan"). In such cases, the development implementer, other than the head of the local government of the previous site, shall consult in advance with the head of the local government of the previous site, and shall submit the formulated development plan to the head of the local government of the previous site without delay.
  (2) When the head of the local government of the previous site formulates or receives a development plan pursuant to paragraph (1), he or she shall publicly notify it as prescribed by Presidential Decree and make it available for public inspection; provided, the information subject to non-disclosure under Article 9(1) of the Official Information Disclosure Act may not be disclosed.
  (3) A development project implementer may modify a development plan directly or at the request of the head of the local government of the previous site. <Amended on Jan. 31, 2025>
  (4) Where a development plan is modified pursuant to paragraph (3), the latter part of paragraph (1) and paragraph (2) shall apply mutatis mutandis to the procedures therefor; provided, this shall not apply where minor matters prescribed by Presidential Decree are modified.

Article 16 (Formulation of implementation plan for previous site development project) (1) When a development plan is formulated and publicly notified pursuant to Article 15, the development project implementer shall formulate an implementation plan for the development project of the previous site (hereinafter referred to as "implementation plan for the previous site development project"), including matters prescribed by Presidential Decree, such as design documents and financing plans necessary for the implementation of the development project of the previous site. In such cases, the development project implementer, other than the head of the local government of the previous site, shall consult in advance with the head of the local government of the local government of the previous site, and submit the implementation plan for the development project of the previous site formulated to the head of the local government of the local government of the previous site without delay.
  (2) The implementation plan for the previous site development project may be formulated in phases.
  (3) The implementation plan for the previous site development project shall reflect matters necessary for improvement, etc. under Article 16(4) of the Urban Traffic Improvement Promotion Act and the results of environmental impact assessment under the Environmental Impact Assessment Act.
  (4) When the head of the local government of the previous site formulates or receives an implementation plan for previous site development project pursuant to paragraph (1), the head shall publicly notify it as prescribed by Presidential Decree and make it available for public inspection; provided, the information subject to non-disclosure under Article 9(1) of the Official Information Disclosure Act may not be disclosed.
  (5) Where a development project implementer modifies an implementation plan for the previous site development project formulated pursuant to paragraphs (1) through (3), the latter part of paragraph (1) and paragraph (4) shall apply mutatis mutandis to the procedures for such modification; provided, this shall not apply where minor matters prescribed by Presidential Decree are modified. <Added on Jan. 31, 2025>

Article 17 (Legal fiction of authorization, permission for implementation plans for previous site development projects) (1) When an implementation plan for a previous site development project is publicly notified pursuant to Article 16(4), the following authorization, permission, etc. shall be deemed granted, and authorization, permission, etc. under the following Acts shall be deemed publicly notified or announced:
  1. Deliberation by the Building Committees under Article 4 of the Building Act, building permission under Article 11 of that Act, notification of building construction under Article 14 of that Act, change to matters permitted and reported under Article 16 of that Act, building permission for temporary buildings under Article 20 of that Act, and consultation about building under Article 29 of that Act;
  2. A permission to extract aggregate under Article 22 of the Aggregate Extraction Act;
  3. Permission to occupy or use of public waters under Article 8 of the Public Waters Management and Reclamation Act, consultation or approval under Article 10 of that Act, authorization of an implementation plan for occupancy or use under Article 17 of that Act, a reclamation license for public waters under Article 28 of that Act, public notice under Article 33 of that Act, consultation on or approval of reclamation conducted by the State, etc. under Article 35 of that Act, approval of an implementation plan for reclamation of public waters under Article 38 of that Act, and approval of a change in the purpose of reclamation under Article 49 of that Act;
  4. Approval of business plans under Article 15 of the Tourism Promotion Act, designation of tourist destinations under Article 52 of that Act, approval of development plans under Article 54 of that Act, and permission to perform development projectS under Article 55 of that Act;
  5. Formulation of implementation plans for intelligent transport systems under Article 76 of the National Transport System Efficiency Act and formulation and approval of implementation plans under Article 79 of that Act;
  6. Permission for using administrative property under Article 30 of the State Property Act;
  7. Determination of urban or Gun management planS under Article 30 of the National Land Planning and Utilization Act; permission for development activities under Article 56 of that Act; determination of the operator of an urban or Gun planning facility project under Article 86 of that Act; and authorization of implementation plans under Article 88 of that Act;
  8. Permission to use agricultural infrastructure under Article 23 of the Agricultural and Fishing Villages Improvement Act; and approval of a project plan to develop a rural tourism and resort complex under Article 82(2) of that Act;
  9. Permission or consultation on the diversion of farmland under Article 34 of the Farmland Act; reporting on the diversion of farmland under Article 35 of that Act; or permission for or consultation on a temporary use of farmland for another purpose under Article 36 of that Act;
  10. Permission for or reporting on installation of emission facilities under Article 23 of the Clean Air Conservation Act, Article 33 of the Water Environment Conservation Act, and Article 8 of Noise and Vibration Control Act;
  11. Designation of an implementer of an urban development project prescribed in Article 11 of the Urban Development Act or approval for an implementation plan prescribed in Article 17 of that Act;
  12. Permission to implement road works by persons other than road management authorities under Article 36 of Road Act, permission to occupy and use roads under Article 61 of that Act, and consultation with or approval from the road management authority under Article 107 of that Act Consultation with or approval by a road management agency under Article 36 of that Act (limited to designation and public notice of road routes under Article 19 of that Act, determination of road zones under Article 25 of that Act, permission to implement road works by persons other than road management authorities under Article 36 of that Act, and permission to occupy and use roads under Article 61 of that Act);
  13. Permission for opening a private road prescribed in Article 4 of the Private Road Act;
  14. Permission for cutting trees or other activities prescribed in Article 14 of the Erosion Control Work Act or cancellation of designation of an erosion control area prescribed in Article 20 of that Act;
  15. Permission for and reporting on activities within forest conservation zones (excluding forest genetic resources protection zones) under Article 9(2)1 and 2 of the Forest Protection Act; revocation of the designation of a forest conservation zone under Article 11(1)1 of that Act; reporting on afforestation, felling, etc. of State forests under Article 9(3) of the State Forest Administration and Management Act; permission for and reporting on felling standing timber, etc. of Forests under Article 36 of the Creation and Management of Forest Resources Act;
  16. Designation of the implementer of industrial complex development projects referred to in Article 16 of the Industrial Sites and Development Act and approval for implementation plans for national industrial complex development, general industrial complex development, and urban high-tech industrial complex development referred to in Articles 17,18, and 18-2 of that Act;
  17. Approval of, and report on, construction, etc. of factory referred to in Article 13(1) of the Industrial Cluster Development and Factory Establishment Act;
  18. Change or cancellation of preserved mountainous districts under Article 6 of the Mountainous Districts Management Act, cancellation of designation of restricted areas for diversion or temporary use of mountainous districts under Article 11 of that Act, permission for diversion of mountainous districts under Article 14 of that Act, and reporting on diversion of mountainous districts under Article 15 of that Act, permission for or reporting on temporary use of mountainous districts under Article 15-2 of that Act, and permission for collection of earth or stone under Article 25 of that Act;
  19. Approval of a comprehensive plan for maintaining small rivers under Article 6 of the Small River Maintenance Act, permission to maintain small rivers, etc. under Article 10 of the same Act, and permission to occupy and use small rivers, etc. under Article 14 of the same Act
  20. Designation and modification of water-source protection area under Article 7 of the Water Supply and Waterworks Installation Act; authorization for general waterworks business under Article 17(1) of that Act; authorization for industrial waterworks business under Article 49 of that Act; authorization for private-use waterworks under Article 52 of that Act; and authorization to install private-use industrial waterworks under Article 54 of that Act;
  21. Consultation about a plan for use of energy under Article 10 of the Energy Use Rationalization Act;
  22. Designation of logistics complexes under Article 22 of the Act on the Development and Management of Logistics Facilities and approval of, or consultation on, an implementation plan for the development of a logistics complex under Article 28 of that Act;
  23. Permission for reburials of graves under Article 27 of the Act on Funeral Services;
  24. Approval or reporting of plans for works for establishing electric installations for private use under Article 8 of the Electrical Safety Management Act;
  25. Approval of a project plan referred to in Article 15 of the Housing Act;
  26. Permission to use or profit from administrative property under Article 20(1) of the Public Property and Commodity Management Act;
  27. Reporting on commencement, change and completion of a project prescribed in Article 86(1) of the Act on the Establishment and Management of Spatial Data;
  28. Consultation about the appropriateness of integrated energy supply prescribed in Article 4 of the Integrated Energy Supply Act;
  29. Approval of a business plan under Article 12 of the Installation and Utilization of Sports Facilities Act;
  30. Permission for changing the form and quality of land, etc. prescribed in Article 21-2 of the Grassland Act, and permission or consultation for conversion of grassland prescribed in Article 23 of that Act;
  31. Approval for or reports on waste disposal facilities under Article 29 of the Wastes Control Act;
  32. Authorization for the installation of public sewerage system (referring only to waste treatment plants) under Article 11 of the Sewerage Act, permission to implement works of public sewerage systems under Article 16 of that Act, permission for occupation and use under Article 24 of that Act or report on installation of a private sewage treatment facility under Article 34(2) of that Act;
  33. Consultation with or approval by a river management agency prescribed in Article 6 of the River Act, permission for implementation of a river project or authorization of an implementation plan for a river project prescribed in Article 30 of that Act, or permission to occupy and use a river prescribed in Article 33 of that Act;
  34. Establishment of a land development plan pursuant to Article 8 of the Land Development Promotion Act and approval of a land development project implementation plan pursuant to Article 9 of that Act;
  35. Review of statements of traffic impact assessment referred to in Article 16 of the Urban Traffic Improvement Promotion Act;
  36. Registration of the opening of a large-scale store under Article 8 of the Distribution Industry Development Act.
  (2) Where it is deemed that authorization, permission, etc. have been granted pursuant to paragraph (1), the fee, service charge, or similar imposed pursuant to a relevant Act or municipal ordinance of the competent local government shall be waived.

Article 18 (Designation of special zones for previous sites) (1) The head of a central administrative agency or the head of a local government of the previous site may designate the previous site as any of the following special zones, as prescribed by relevant statutes:
  1. A special tourist zone referred to in Article 70 of the Tourism Promotion Act;
  2. Special building zones under Article 69 of the Building Act;
  3. A free economic zone referred to in Article 4 of the Special Act on Designation and Management of Free Economic Zones;
  4. Regulation-free special zones and special economic zones for specialized regional development under Article 2 of the Act on Special Cases concerning the Regulation of Regulation-Free Special Zones and Special Economic Zones for Specialized Regional Development;
  5. A specialized complex for smart cities defined in subparagraph 6 of Article 29 of the Act on the Promotion of Smart City Development and Industry;
  6. Special research and development zones under Article 4 of the Special Act on Promotion of Special Research and Development Zones.
  (2) When the head of a central administrative agency designates a special zone referred to in paragraph (1)2 through 6, he or she may hear the opinions of the head of the local government of the previous site.

Article 19 (Installation of infrastructure and preferential support) (1) Article 55 of the Urban Development Act shall apply mutatis mutandis to the installation of facilities for electricity, telecommunications, gas, and district heating, and the allocation of the cost thereof.
  (2) The local government of the previous site may preferentially support the installation of infrastructure in the area adjacent to the previous site so that the functions of the city in which the previous site is located can be facilitated smoothly.

CHAPTER IV SUPPORT FOR CONSTRUCTION PROJECTS FOR INTEGRATED NEW AIRPORT AND DEVELOPMENT PROJECTS OF PREVISOUS SITE

Article 20 (Government's financial support) (1) Where necessary for a construction project for an integrated new airport, the State may subsidize or loan necessary expenses to a project implementer under Article 8 within budgetary limits.
  (2) Notwithstanding Article 55 of the State Property Act and Article 9 of the Special Act on Relocation of and Support for Military Air Base Relocation and Article 9 of the Special Act on Relocation of and Support for Military Air Base Relocation, where the project cost exceeds the value of property disused in the course of implementing a military air base relocation project and a project for supporting the environs of the relocation site, the State may subsidize the project implementer within budgetary limits at the request of the head of the relevant central government agency.
  (3) The detailed scope, scale, procedures, methods, etc. of support under paragraph (2) shall be prescribed by Presidential Decree.

Article 21 (Reduction of and exemption from charges) Where necessary to facilitate the execution of an integrated new airport construction project and a development project for the previous site, the State and local governments may reduce or exempt development charges, farmland conservation charges, alternative grassland creation costs, substitute grassland creation costs, substitute forest resources creation costs, river occupancy or use charges, charges for causing traffic congestion, ecosystem conservation charges, public waters occupancy or use charges, environmental improvement charges, infrastructure-building fees, charges on intercity transport facilities of a project implementer or a development project implementer under Article 8, as prescribed by the Restitution of Development Gains Act, the Farmland Act, the Grassland Act, the Mountainous Districts Management Act, the River Act, the Urban Traffic Improvement Promotion Act, Natural Environment Conservation Act, Public Waters Management and Reclamation Act, Public Waters Management and Reclamation Act, Environmental Improvement Cost Liability Act, National Land Planning and Utilization Act, and Special Act on the Management of Intercity Transportation in Metropolitan Areas.

Article 22 (Private capital inducement) The implementer and the development project implementer referred to in Article 8(1) may induce private capital for the integrated new airport construction project and the previous site development project, as prescribed by the Act on Public-Private Partnerships in Infrastructure.

Article 23 (Support for projects to induce private capital) (1) The State and a metropolitan local government may provide support the following matters to private developers who implement a project to induce private capital in an area where the integrated new airport construction project and the previous site development project are implemented:
  1. Permission to occupy and use public facilities;
  2. Acting as an agent to purchase land, facilities, etc. necessary for a project;
  3. Granting a business right to develop neighboring land prescribed by Presidential Decree to the extent to which the profitability of private developers is guaranteed;
  4. Other activities prescribed by Presidential Decree.
  (2) Where there is a person authorized to grant permission to occupy and use public facilities under paragraph (1)1, the State or a metropolitan local government may request the relevant authorized person to grant permission to occupy and use. Upon receipt of such request, the person shall comply therewith, except in extenuating circumstances.

Article 24 (Financial support for foreign-invested companies) (1) The State and local governments of the previous site may provide financial support to foreign-invested companies defined in Article 2(1)6 of the Foreign Investment Promotion Act (hereinafter referred to as "relocating foreign-invested companies") which move into an area where the previous site development project is implemented. In such cases, Article 14-2 of the Foreign Investment Promotion Act shall apply mutatis mutandis to matters necessary for the eligibility, scale, procedures, etc. for such support.
  (2) The State and local governments of the previous site may purchase land for which permission for use, etc. is granted or construct buildings for which permission for use, etc. is granted, in order to attract relocating foreign-invested companies.

Article 25 (Preferential treatment of local companies) Where a project implementer or a development project implementer under Article 8 enters into a contract for construction works, goods, services, etc. prescribed by Presidential Decree, such implementer may give preferential treatment to a person who has his or her principal place of business in an area where the integrated new airport construction project or the previous site development project is implemented, as prescribed by Presidential Decree.

Article 26 (Preferential employment and participation of local residents) The project implementer under Article 8 may preferentially employ migrants and residents of the environs of the relocation site following the integrated new airport construction project or have them participate therein.

Article 27 (Special cases concerning installation, use of sports facilities) Notwithstanding Article 11(2) of the Installation and Utilization of Sports Facilities Act, a project implementer and a development project implementer referred to in Article 8 may install sports facilities in an area where the relevant project is implemented, if necessary for the integrated new airport construction project and the previous site development project.

Article 28 (Special cases concerning creation of industrial complexes) Upon receipt of a request from the head of the relevant metropolitan local government, the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport may change the type of an industrial complex by altering the functions of all or part of an industrial complex in order to revitalize an industrial complex in an area where an integrated new airport construction project or a previous site development project is implemented. In such cases, Article 13-2 of the Industrial Sites and Development Act shall apply to the requirements, procedures, etc. for change.

Article 29 (Special cases concerning implementation of preliminary feasibility study) Notwithstanding Article 38(1) of the National Finance Act, the Minister of Planning and Budget may exempt a person from a preliminary feasibility study, if deemed necessary for the prompt and smooth implementation of the integrated new airport construction project. <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025.>

Article 29-2 (Special cases concerning issuance of local government bonds) A local government may issue local government bonds for the integrated new airport construction project and the previous site development project. In such cases, notwithstanding Article 11 of the Local Finance Act, it may issue local government bonds in excess of the maximum amount of local government bonds to be issued.
  [Added on Jan. 31, 2025]

Article 30 (Special cases concerning the Immigration Act) Notwithstanding Articles 8,10-2, and 10-3 of the Immigration Act, the Minister of Justice may separately prescribe procedures for issuing visas to foreigners who work for companies located in an area where the previous site development project is implemented and the maximum period of sojourn for each status of sojourn.

CHAPTER V SUPPLEMENTARY PROVISIONS

Article 31 (Delegation of authority) The Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport may delegate part of his or her authority under this Act to the head of a metropolitan local government having jurisdiction over an area where the integrated new airport construction project and the previous site development project are implemented, as prescribed by Presidential Decree.

Article 32 (Reporting and inspection) (1) Where necessary for the enforcement of this Act, the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport may require an implementer under Article 8(2) to submit a necessary report or data on the integrated new airport construction project (excluding a military air base relocation project; hereafter the same shall apply in this Article through Article 35 and Article 38) and may require public officials under his or her control to enter the office, place of business, or other necessary places of the relevant implementer to inspect affairs concerning the integrated new airport construction project.
  (2) Where necessary for the enforcement of this Act, the head of the local government of the previous site may require the development project implementer to file a necessary report or submit data concerning the development project of the previous site, and may have public officials under his or her jurisdiction enter the office, place of business, and other necessary places of the development project implementer to inspect affairs concerning the development project of the previous site.
  (3) Any public official who inspects affairs concerning the integrated new airport construction project or the previous site development project under paragraph (1) or (2) shall carry a certificate indicating his or her authority and present it to interested persons.
  (4) Matters necessary for the identification referred to in paragraph (3) shall be prescribed by Presidential Decree.

Article 33 (Corrective orders) In any of the following cases, the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport may order the implementer of the integrated new airport construction project, other than the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport, to take appropriate measures:
  1. Where the person fails to begin the construction within one year from the due date for commencement of the construction stated in the application for the approval of implementation plan or fails to complete the construction by the due date for completion of the construction without good cause;
  2. Where the facilities that have completed construction works differ from the details of approval of an implementation plan as a result of the confirmation of completion of construction under Article 20(1) of the Airport Facilities Act, which is applied mutatis mutandis in Article 5(3);
  3. Where the person violates the conditions attached to the permission.

Article 34 (Revocation of permission) (1) Where the integrated new airport construction project implementer other than the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport falls under any of the following, the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport may cancel the permission or approval under this Act or take necessary measures such as an order to suspend the effect thereof or to cease the construction; provided, the Minister shall cancel the permission or approval regarding the implementation and management of such project in cases of subparagraph 1 or 4:
  1. Where permission or approval has been obtained by fraud or other improper means;
  2. Where it formulates an implementation plan or modifies approved matters without obtaining approval, in violation of Article 7(3) of the Airport Facilities Act applied mutatis mutandis in Article 5(3);
  3. Where the implementer violates an implementation plan approved or approved for modification under Article 7(3) of the Airport Facilities Act as applied mutatis mutandis in Article 5(3);
  4. Where it is deemed impossible to continue the integrated new airport construction project due to changes in circumstances;
  5. Where a person ordered to take corrective measures under Article 33 fails to take appropriate measures within a reasonable period prescribed by the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport.
  (2) Upon issuing a disposition or order under paragraph (1), the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport shall publicly notify such fact, as prescribed by Presidential Decree.
  (3) Detailed standards for dispositions under paragraph (1) and other necessary matters shall be prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport.

Article 35 (Imposition of penalty surcharges) (1) Where the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport is required to order the integrated new airport construction project implementer, other than the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport, to suspend the effect of permission or approval for the implementation and management of the project or to suspend construction works pursuant to Article 34, and where such disposition is likely to cause serious inconvenience to users of the relevant facilities or to infringe on the public interest, the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport may impose and collect a penalty surcharge not exceeding one billion won in lieu of such disposition.
  (2) Matters necessary for the types of violation for which penalty surcharges are imposed under paragraph (1) and the amount of such penalty surcharges according to the degree of violation shall be prescribed by Presidential Decree.
  (3) Where a person slapped with penalty surcharges under paragraph (1) fails to pay the penalty surcharges by the payment due date, the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport shall collect the amount in the same manner as forced collection of national taxes.

Article 36 (Hearings) Where the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport intends to revoke permission or approval pursuant to Article 34, the Minister shall hold a hearing.

CHAPTER VI PENALTY PROVISIONS

Article 37 (Violation of orders) Any of the following persons shall be punished by imprisonment with labor for not more than one year or by a fine not exceeding 10 million won:
  1. A person who conducts acts such as the construction of buildings without obtaining permission or permission of change for matters which require permission or permission of change under Article 10(1) applied mutatis mutandis in Article 5(3) or who obtains permission by fraud or other improper means;
  2. A person who interferes with or refuses an act under Article 11(1) of the Airport Facilities Act applied mutatis mutandis in Article 5(3), without good cause;
  3. A person who violates an order or disposition under Article 33 or 34(1) without good cause.

Article 38 (Crime of unlawful use of facilities following integrated new airport construction project) Any of following persons shall be punished by a fine not exceeding 20 million won:
  1. Any person who uses a facility in violation of Article 20(7) of the Airport Facilities Act applied mutatis mutandis in Article 5(3);
  2. A person who violates Article 56(1) or (2) of the Airport Facilities Act applied mutatis mutandis in Article 5(3);
  3. A person who installs facilities without obtaining permission, in violation of Article 8(2);
  4. A person who uses facilities for which the permission was canceled under Article 34.

Article 39 (Crimes of business interference) A person who refuses, interferes with, or obstructs a report or inspection under Article 32(1), or makes a false report or false information, shall be punished by a fine not exceeding 5 million won.

Article 40 (Crime of non-compliance with order to restrain or evict) Any person who fails to comply with an order issued under Article 56(7) of the Airport Facilities Act applied mutatis mutandis pursuant to Article 5(3) shall be punished by a fine not exceeding 200,000 won, by misdemeanor imprisonment, or by a minor fine. In such cases, Articles 71 through 74 of the Airport Facilities Act shall apply to procedures for dealing with offenses.

Article 41 (Joint penalty provisions) If the representative of a corporation or an agent or employee of, or any other person employed, by a corporation or an individual commits any violation described in Articles 37 through 40 in performing any work for the corporation or individual, the corporation or individual shall, in addition to punishing the violator accordingly, be punished by a fine prescribed in the relevant Article; provided, the same shall not apply where the corporation or individual has not neglected to exercise due care and supervise the work to prevent such violation.

